{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JfgvpDrwDvMoaSoR3zWWjp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\ttitle: Composite types\n3\tdescription: Work with composite types and embedded documents in MongoDB\n4\turl: /orm/v7/prisma-client/special-fields-and-types/composite-types\n5\tmetaTitle: Composite types\n6\tmetaDescription: Composite types\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t:::warning\n10\t\n11\tComposite types are only available with MongoDB.\n12\t\n13\t:::\n14\t\n15\t[Composite types](/orm/v7/prisma-schema/data-model/models), known as [embedded documents](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/data-modeling/#embedded-data) in MongoDB, allow you to embed records within other records.\n16\t\n17\tThis page explains how to:\n18\t\n19\t- [find](#finding-records-that-contain-composite-types-with-find-and-findmany) records that contain composite types using `findFirst` and `findMany`\n20\t- [create](#creating-records-with-composite-types-using-create-and-createmany) new records with composite types using `create` and `createMany`\n21\t- [update](#changing-composite-types-within-update-and-updatemany) composite types within existing records using `update` and `updateMany`\n22\t- [delete](#deleting-records-that-contain-composite-types-with-delete-and-deletemany) records with composite types using `delete` and `deleteMany`\n23\t\n24\t## Example schema\n25\t\n26\tWe’ll use this schema for the examples that follow:\n27\t\n28\t```prisma title=\"schema.prisma\" showLineNumbers\n29\tgenerator client {\n30\t  provider = \"prisma-client-js\"\n31\t}\n32\t\n33\tdatasource db {\n34\t  provider = \"mongodb\"\n35\t  url      = env(\"DATABASE_URL\")\n36\t}\n37\t\n38\tmodel Product {\n39\t  id     String  @id @default(auto()) @map(\"_id\") @db.ObjectId\n40\t  name   String  @unique\n41\t  price  Float\n42\t  colors Color[]\n43\t  sizes  Size[]\n44\t  photos Photo[]\n45\t  orders Order[]\n46\t}\n47\t\n48\tmodel Order {\n49\t  id              String   @id @default(auto()) @map(\"_id\") @db.ObjectId\n50\t  product         Product  @relation(fields: [productId], references: [id])\n51\t  color           Color\n52\t  size            Size\n53\t  shippingAddress Address\n54\t  billingAddress  Address?\n55\t  productId       String   @db.ObjectId\n56\t}\n57\t\n58\tenum Color {\n59\t  Red\n60\t  Green\n61\t  Blue\n62\t}\n63\t\n64\tenum Size {\n65\t  Small\n66\t  Medium\n67\t  Large\n68\t  XLarge\n69\t}\n70\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a7eb42c3-e898-44f8-9d9c-feef5da0c48f","uuid":"7542c81a-4812-4018-879d-bd7d821c77db","timestamp":"2026-09-24T21:54:30.105Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/jcarr/.cache/markdownattractor/bench/prisma/apps/docs/content/docs/orm/v7/prisma-client/special-fields-and-types/composite-types.mdx","content":"---\ntitle: Composite types\ndescription: Work with composite types and embedded documents in MongoDB\nurl: /orm/v7/prisma-client/special-fields-and-types/composite-types\nmetaTitle: Composite types\nmetaDescription: Composite types\n---\n\n:::warning\n\nComposite types are only available with MongoDB.\n\n:::\n\n[Composite types](/orm/v7/prisma-schema/data-model/models), known as [embedded documents](https://www.mongodb.com/docs/manual/data-modeling/#embedded-data) in MongoDB, allow you to embed records within other records.\n\nThis page explains how to:\n\n- [find](#finding-records-that-contain-composite-types-with-find-and-findmany) records that contain composite types using `findFirst` and `findMany`\n- [create](#creating-records-with-composite-types-using-create-and-createmany) new records with composite types using `create` and `createMany`\n- [update](#changing-composite-types-within-update-and-updatemany) composite types within existing records using `update` and `updateMany`\n- [delete](#deleting-records-that-contain-composite-types-with-delete-and-deletemany) records with composite types using `delete` and `deleteMany`\n\n## Example schema\n\nWe’ll use this schema for the examples that follow:\n\n```prisma title=\"schema.prisma\" showLineNumbers\ngenerator client {\n  provider = \"prisma-client-js\"\n}\n\ndatasource db {\n  provider = \"mongodb\"\n  url      = env(\"DATABASE_URL\")\n}\n\nmodel Product {\n  id     String  @id @default(auto()) @map(\"_id\") @db.ObjectId\n  name   String  @unique\n  price  Float\n  colors Color[]\n  sizes  Size[]\n  photos Photo[]\n  orders Order[]\n}\n\nmodel Order {\n  id              String   @id @default(auto()) @map(\"_id\") @db.ObjectId\n  product         Product  @relation(fields: [productId], references: [id])\n  color           Color\n  size            Size\n  shippingAddress Address\n  billingAddress  Address?\n  productId       String   @db.ObjectId\n}\n\nenum Color {\n  Red\n  Green\n  Blue\n}\n\nenum Size {\n  Small\n  Medium\n  Large\n  XLarge\n}\n","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":783}}}
